          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            For a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            its
            %em topological complexity
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi TC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TC(X)
            is the smallest number
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi k
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U_k)_{k=1}^n
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times X
            by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
            addmitting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+sections"} local sections
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_k\colon X\times X\rightarrow P X
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evaluation+map"} evaluation map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                          %mo ×
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi γ
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mi γ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi γ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  P X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X\times X
                  \\\
                  \\gamma &amp;\mapsto&amp; \big(\gamma(0),\gamma(1)\big)
                  }
          %p
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+space"} path space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P X
          %p
            It is also possible to define it using the
            %span.newWikiWord
              Schwarz genus
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Schwarz+genus"} ?
            of the path space fibration
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi P
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega X\hookrightarrow P X\rightarrow X
          %p
            There is also the convention of using the smallest number
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi k
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U_k)_{k=0}^n
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+sets"} open sets
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times X
            with the above property exists. This lowers all topological complexities by one, hence the convention used can be given by giving the topological complexity of the set with one point. (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi TC
